draw((19,4)--(16,1),EndArrow);
draw((16,0)--(24,0),EndArrow);
draw((24,1)--(21,4),EndArrow);
</asy>

Any team from group <imath>L</imath> that won a team from group <imath>W</imath> will form a cycle with <imath>A</imath>. Now we need to count how many teams in group <imath>L</imath> won over a team from group <imath>W</imath>. The total number of wins in group <imath>L</imath> is <imath>10 \cdot 10 =100</imath>. There are <imath>\tbinom{10}2=45</imath> wins among the teams inside group <imath>L</imath>. So group <imath>L</imath> has <imath>100-45=55</imath> wins over group <imath>W</imath>.

<cmath>\frac{21 \cdot 55}{3}=\boxed{385, \textbf{(A)}}</cmath>

