'''Step 1:''' To find the total number of paths, observe that all paths will have <imath>10</imath> total steps. We have to choose which <imath>5</imath> of these steps will be NE (the rest will be NW). So the total number of paths is <imath>\binom{10}{5}</imath>. 
The formula for [[Combination|combinations]] is: <imath>\binom{n}{r} = \frac{n!}{r!(n-r)!}</imath> and <imath>\binom{10}{5} = \frac{10!}{5!\times5!}=252</imath>.

'''Step 2:''' Each path splits the total area of <imath>25</imath> in two parts. So, for any path that gives area = <imath>A</imath>, you can find a unique "''sister''" path that has an area = <imath>25-A</imath> (in other words, the pair of paths have a combined area of 25).  Possible ways to define the "''sister''" path are: 
