'''Step 3:''' There are a few ways to get from this observation to the total area: 
*There are <imath>252/2 = 126</imath> pairs of such paths, and the total area of each pair is <imath>25</imath>.  So the total area given by all paths is <imath>126 \times 25</imath>. 
*Each of the <imath>252</imath> paths gives an area of <imath>25</imath> if you also count the "''sister''" paths. Since each "''sister''" path is also one of the <imath>252</imath>, you have to divide by <imath>2</imath> to avoid double counting.  So the total area given by all paths is <imath>\frac{252 \times 25}{2}</imath>.
